<heading>events list - Show the runtime's history.</heading>

<rule/>

<heading level="2">
Usage
</heading>

<pre>
  events list [--limit N]
</pre>

<heading level="2">
Description
</heading>

<paragraph>
Lists the activity events recorded by the runtime, newest first (default
20). An event records what a session did, asked for, or was refused — a
read, a denied operation, a login failure, or a completed command.
</paragraph>

<paragraph>
Every event is written by the runtime itself, never by a command. There is
no legitimate way to change state without the runtime knowing (ADR-17).
</paragraph>

<heading level="2">
See also
</heading>

<paragraph>
events show, man
</paragraph>
